     "body": "<p>I'll note that I only caught this because the purgeDatastream tests for fedora-client were intermittently failing, as fedora-client does handle xsd:dateTimes correctly. See <a href=\"http://github.com/mediashelf/fedora-client/blob/master/src/main/java/com/yourmediashelf/fedora/util/DateUtility.java\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://github.com/mediashelf/fedora-client/blob/master/src/main/java/com/yourmediashelf/fedora/util/DateUtility.java</a> for what I believe is a correct implementation, but it's a complete re-write that doesn't use SimpleDateFormat.</p>",
